            "control-effectiveness": "none",
            "maestro-layer": "L7 \u2014 Agent Ecosystem",
            "inherent-risk": "8.2",
            "residual-risk": "8.2",
            "recommendation": "Implement access control for partner-feed. Evaluate the original caller's entitlement for each object and action, and deny by default when the check cannot be made. Place the control where signed carrier manifests are first received, so that nothing downstream has to repeat the check. This addresses: A compromised peer presents a forged service identity to partner-feed, and partner-feed accepts the claim without verifying the signature chain back to the issuing authority. Acceptance check: a caller without the entitlement is denied for every object and action, including through indirect paths, and the denial is recorded. Apply the change to the most exposed instances first, then to the rest, and keep the previous configuration available for a quick rollback. Suggested location: stub-codebase/src/partner_feed/access_control.py. Reference patterns: Role and attribute checks at the service boundary, deny-by-default policy.",
            "effort-estimate": "High"
          }
