            "inherent-risk": "8.1",
            "residual-risk": "6.1",
            "recommendation": "Harden the existing authentication control: verify the caller's signed credential on every request to this component and bind it to the channel it arrived on on the paths of edge-gateway that it does not yet cover. The current implementation is recorded at src/gateway/token_verify.py:7 and covers the main request path. Extend it to the secondary paths and add a test that exercises each of them. This addresses: A shared or long-lived bearer token on edge-gateway lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. Acceptance check: a request that carries a missing, expired or mismatched credential is rejected with a logged reason, and a valid request still succeeds. Coordinate the change with the owners of dependent services so that none of them relies on the behaviour being removed. Suggested location: src/gateway/token_verify.py. Reference patterns: Short-lived signed tokens, mutual TLS, workload identity.",
