          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "3.2",
            "control-status": "partial",
            "control-evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/store/queries.py",
                "line": 8,
                "snippet": "def load_task(conn, task_id):\n    cur = conn.cursor()\n    cur.execute(\"select body from tasks where id = %s\", (task_id,))\n    row = cur.fetchone()\n    return row[0] if row else None"
              }
            ],
            "control-carry-forward": false,
            "control-effectiveness": "weak",
            "maestro-layer": "L2 \u2014 Data Operations",
            "inherent-risk": "4.3",
            "residual-risk": "3.2",
            "recommendation": "Harden the existing input validation control: validate each structured input against a closed schema before use, and reject unknown fields and oversized values on the paths of vector-store-a that it does not yet cover. The current implementation is recorded at src/store/queries.py:8 and covers the main request path. Extend it to the secondary paths and add a test that exercises each of them. This addresses: Serialised objects arriving from worker-2 are deserialised by vector-store-a with permissive type handling, allowing crafted payloads to instantiate unintended behaviour. Acceptance check: malformed, oversized and unexpected fields are rejected before any side effect, and a regression test covers each rejected shape. Roll the change out behind a flag, watch error rates for one release and remove the flag once no regression is seen. Suggested location: src/store/queries.py. Reference patterns: Schema validation, parameterised queries, output encoding.",
            "effort-estimate": "Low"
          }
        },
