            "recommendation": "Implement logging/audit for worker-3. Record who did what, to which object, with which outcome, in a store that operators cannot alter. Place the control where work orders and draft documents are first received, so that nothing downstream has to repeat the check. This addresses: Operators approve changes to work orders and draft documents through a chat message or ticket comment that is not bound to the executed change, so approvals can be disputed. Acceptance check: every state change produces one complete record that an operator cannot edit, and a gap in the sequence raises an alert. Ship to the internal environment first, compare behaviour with the previous release and promote after reviewing the first week of records. Suggested location: stub-codebase/src/worker_3/logging_audit.py. Reference patterns: Append-only ledger, hash chaining, structured events.",
