            "recommendation": "Harden the existing logging/audit control: record who did what, to which object, with which outcome, in a store that operators cannot alter on the paths of planner-agent that it does not yet cover. The current implementation is recorded at src/audit/ledger_writer.py:9 and covers the main request path. Extend it to the secondary paths and add a test that exercises each of them. This addresses: Clock drift between planner-agent and router-agent leaves events in inconsistent order, so the sequence of actions on task plans and tool selections cannot be reconstructed reliably. Acceptance check: every state change produces one complete record that an operator cannot edit, and a gap in the sequence raises an alert. Coordinate the change with the owners of dependent services so that none of them relies on the behaviour being removed. Suggested location: src/audit/ledger_writer.py. Reference patterns: Append-only ledger, hash chaining, structured events.",
